# Known divergence (by design): this test defines qnodes(), a helper whose body
# runs a dynamic EXECUTE ('EXPLAIN ' || query) the gateway cannot vet, so its
# CREATE is rejected. Each PostGIS test creates and DROPs its own qnodes, so it
# is re-seeded directly on the primary before every test
# (testdata/pg17/external/postgis_preseed.sql, applied by the patched
# run_test.pl); the index checks then run and only the rejected CREATE remains.
#
# A few operators additionally pick a different scan type (Seq vs Index) than
# PostGIS's expected output: gist/spgist cost estimation differs slightly through
# the pooler even with the planner GUCs normalized to PostgreSQL defaults.
